  "notes": "Surface derived 2026-07-28 from the W3C Screen Capture WD 2026-07-23 (rendered, anchors live) and Chromium trunk IDL/flags/picker source: exactly one new dictionary member (audioSelection) + one single-value enum (AudioSelectionPreferenceEnum) added to the existing getDisplayMedia options dictionary, plus the observable desktop-picker steering behavior that constitutes the feature's effect. No new interfaces, methods, events, track constraints, or readable state exist. Naming: the chromestatus listing/I2S say 'audioPreferred'/'audioPreference'; the shipped member is audioSelection \u2014 documented explicitly on the page. The Editor's Draft at w3c.github.io serves the merged sections with unexpanded Bikeshed macros and no fragment anchors as of 2026-07-28; the page cites the dated WD for verbatim text and notes the ED state. No upstream WPT coverage; no BCD entry \u2014 compat tables are interim, compiled from primary sources and labelled as such. Runtime picker behavior verified from desktop_media_picker_views.cc at trunk, not executed locally (local Chrome is older than 152)."
